<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-inner"><div class="eyebrow">Kev, pull up a chair. This one's for Salesfire.</div><h1>NOT ANOTHER<br/><span class="red">SPONSOR DECK.</span></h1><p class="lead">A backstage invitation to help create the kind of ecommerce media, live experiences and wonderfully strange ideas people actually remember.</p><div class="chips"><span>UK + US ecommerce</span><span>Real conversations</span><span>Original comedy</span></div><a class="button" href="#the-world">Take the tour ↘</a></div></section>
<div class="strip">LESS GLASS. LESS STEEL. MORE HUMAN BEINGS.</div>
<section class="section wrap" id="the-world"><div class="eyebrow">01 / The world we want to build</div><h2>From the campfire<br/>to the <span class="red">studio lights.</span></h2><p class="intro">Imagine a media partnership that doesn't end with a logo on a thumbnail. A camp where people actually talk. A stage where the audience can look a guest in the eye. A bus where the career stories are as interesting as the success stories.</p><div class="photo-grid">{images.map(image=><div class="photo"><img src={image.src} alt={image.sub} loading="lazy"/><div class="photo-copy"><b>{image.label}</b><span>{image.sub}</span></div></div>)}</div><p class="concept">Visual mood references only — not photographs of confirmed V Spot events. Replace with approved Camp Tralee, live-stage and Struggle Bus photography for the final version.</p></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Why you, why us</div><h2>We've already got <span class="red">history.</span></h2><p class="quote">The best brand partner doesn't interrupt the interesting bit. It helps make the interesting bit happen.</p><p class="intro">Kev and Vinny go back to the retailer days, including Horkans and Seagreen. More recently, Sally shared Salesfire's AI Search work, and the conversation grew into custom creative for the World Cup and a Camp Tralee sponsorship idea. So this isn't an introduction from zero. It's a chance to make something bigger.</p></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Your stages</div><h2>One partner. <span class="red">Multiple worlds.</span></h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">The Struggle Bus</div><h3>People before job titles.</h3><p>Career turns, candid mistakes and honest conversations. A recognisable season sponsor without compromising the guest's story.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">The V Spot News</div><h3>Six minutes you won't get back.</h3><p>Fast ecommerce satire, topical commentary and a distinctive sponsor moment that belongs in the show.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">V Spot PSAs</div><h3>Ads worth watching.</h3><p>Original short-form comedy built around merchant frustrations, product discovery and the absurdities of modern retail.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">The Ostrich Report</div><h3>Dig into marketplaces.</h3><p>Operator-led conversations and cross-border stories. Subject to existing sponsor rights and availability.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Camp Tralee</div><h3>Ideas around a fire.</h3><p>A potential live experience with actual proximity between guests, speakers and attendees. Format and dates to confirm.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Live Specials</div><h3>No conference wallpaper.</h3><p>Close-up stages, entertaining interviews and creative merchant experiences rather than another panel of five chairs.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">04 / Creative starting points</div><h2>Make some <span class="red">beautiful trouble.</span></h2><div class="options"><article><h3>Search Party</h3><p>What shoppers type versus what they mean. A recurring, ridiculous but insightful exploration of product discovery.</p></article><article><h3>The Conversion Confessional</h3><p>Retailers confess their worst onsite experiences and discuss how to fix them, without turning it into a product demo.</p></article><article><h3>AI vs Actual Humans</h3><p>Can a smart search experience understand the world's least articulate shopping request?</p></article><article><h3>Retail Therapy: Live</h3><p>Small-room stories, merchant problems, comedy and a proper conversation at audience level.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">05 / Commercial routes</div><h2>Start small. <span class="red">Think big.</span></h2><div class="grid">{offers.map(o=><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">{o.tier}</div><h3>{o.title}</h3><div class="price">{o.price}</div><p>{o.body}</p></article>)}</div><p class="small">All prices are indicative 2027 discussion ranges, not agreed offers. Final scope, availability, category rights, production costs, event commitments and reporting are subject to written agreement. No audience or performance guarantees are implied.</p></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">06 / The grown-up bit</div><h2>Creative freedom.<br/><span class="red">Commercial clarity.</span></h2><p class="intro">We agree deliverables, approvals, distribution rights, sponsor identification and measurable objectives up front. Editorial independence remains intact. Historic referral discussions are separate from this media partnership. We'll build a verified media kit and confirm existing category commitments before contracting.</p></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">07 / The next scene</div><h2>Kev, let's skip the <span class="red">48-slide deck.</span></h2><p class="lead">What does Salesfire want from 2027 — merchant conversations, brand familiarity, pipeline, category leadership or something else? Give me half an hour and we'll work backwards from the answer.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:vinny@vinnyandco.com?subject=Salesfire%20x%20V%20Spot%20%E2%80%94%202027%20Partner%20Green%20Room">Let's talk 2027 ↗</a></section>
<footer class="footer wrap">THE V SPOT STUDIOS · PRIVATE CREATIVE PROPOSAL · OCTOBER 2026 <p class="small">Concept images are illustrative and not representations of past or confirmed V Spot events. Not a binding offer.</p></footer></main></body></html>